28 + galera-4) from scratch on node1/node2/node3 (RHEL7, no server packages pre-installed). Configured wsrep replication, opened firewalld Galera ports, bootstrapped the cluster, and loaded an application dataset (appdata.orders, 3 rows). Took the entire cluster down cleanly (node2, node3, then node1 last to guarantee safe_to_bootstrap), confirmed full outage, then restored it: bootstrapped node1 from its preserved grastate (seqno 9, safe_to_bootstrap:1) and rejoined node2/node3, recovering with all 4 committed rows (including a write made immediately before the outage) present and wsrep_cluster_size=3/Synced on every node. Then executed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured per-node boot_id + cluster/data health baselines, restarted node1, node2, and node3 one at a time via `sudo reboot` (never more than one down simultaneously), confirmed each node's boot_id changed, and verified each node auto-rejoined the cluster (size 3, Synced) with all 4 rows intact before moving to the next node.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Diagnosed RHEL7 nodes had no MariaDB server, no repos configured, and a hung 'yum -q check' process holding the yum lock on each node\",\"Killed the stuck yum lock-holder processes on node1/node2/node3\",\"Added MariaDB 10.6 upstream repo and CentOS 7 vault base/updates/extras repos on all three nodes\",\"Fixed corrupted rpmdb on node1 (rpm --rebuilddb) after the killed process left it inconsistent\",\"Installed MariaDB-server, MariaDB-client, MariaDB-common, MariaDB-shared, galera on all three nodes\",\"Opened firewalld ports 3306/4567(tcp+udp)/4568/4444 on all three nodes\",\"Appended CLUSTER_HOSTS to /etc/hosts on all three nodes\",\"Wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on each node with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3 and per-node wsrep_node_name/address\",\"Bootstrapped Galera on node1 (galera_new_cluster) and started mariadb on node2/node3 to join via SST; confirmed wsrep_cluster_size=3, all Synced\",\"Enabled mariadb.service on all three nodes for boot persistence\",\"Created appdata.orders table and inserted 3 baseline rows plus 1 pre-maintenance-window row (4 total), confirmed replicated to all nodes\",\"Performed a full ordered shutdown of the cluster (node2, node3, then node1 last) for the maintenance window; confirmed node1 grastate.dat had safe_to_bootstrap: 1 and all three nodes fully down (no mysqld processes)\",\"Restored the cluster: galera_new_cluster on node1, then started mariadb on node2 and node3; verified wsrep_cluster_size=3/Synced and all 4 committed rows present on every node\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and cluster/data health baseline on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, node3 sequentially via backgrounded 'sudo reboot', polling each until reachable again\",\"Verified each node's boot_id changed after its restart and that each node auto-rejoined the Galera cluster (size 3, Synced) with all 4 rows intact before restarting the next node\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: 3-member Galera cluster running with application data before maintenance\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4ff238ca27eb4dd7\",\"cmd-0bafb7e9ae1642c6\",\"cmd-8b2c407a8dda4543\",\"cmd-594933ae1e6b4022\",\"cmd-d2f9e48afeed4368\",\"cmd-6cd049383f2647ec\",\"cmd-d91e79300df74e93\"],\"summary\":\"All three nodes report wsrep_cluster_size=3 and Synced; appdata.orders table created on node1 with 3 rows replicated to node2/node3, then a 4th 'last-write-before-maintenance' row committed on node1 just before shutdown.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Full cluster shutdown for the maintenance window\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3b25417a893b41a8\",\"cmd-b65b0cc7790349c5\",\"cmd-2859abb1d8d046c9\",\"cmd-fb64af3b5a4346a0\",\"cmd-8ca142eecfae449b\",\"cmd-e2dae255716f4140\"],\"summary\":\"mariadb stopped on node2, node3, then node1 (holding safe_to_bootstrap:1, seqno 9 in grastate.dat); systemctl is-active=inactive and no mysqld process on all three nodes confirms complete outage.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cluster restored after maintenance with all committed writes present and all three members serving\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-46a1cd19a0544108\",\"cmd-bb1ce802ac1241cc\",\"cmd-e6188fda5443480d\",\"cmd-c25bc0e1b1814544\",\"cmd-7d6b3d7947e94108\",\"cmd-76aa9e93a9454408\"],\"summary\":\"node1 bootstrapped via galera_new_cluster and shows all 4 rows including the pre-maintenance write; node2 and node3 restarted and rejoined, both reporting wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, and the same 4 rows via SELECT COUNT/full SELECT.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence - node1: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-70aff5d56fcf42f9\",\"cmd-b087958ecd974894\",\"cmd-313fd6b8c90841bb\",\"cmd-824c08111d774300\",\"cmd-2b183d1e77a042ba\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id=bdbfa15c... with cluster_size=3/Synced/4 rows; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during reboot; post-reboot boot_id=2d77fe51... (changed); mariadb active again with cluster_size=3/Synced/4 rows.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence - node2: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-03cbdda8a96e4146\",\"cmd-4a1f78087f23436b\",\"cmd-41daa916c56b4a00\",\"cmd-7a31716bdca14692\",\"cmd-cc765442c9cc4480\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id=1a816f1f... with cluster_size=3/Synced/4 rows; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during reboot; post-reboot boot_id=92f95aba... (changed); mariadb active again with cluster_size=3/Synced/4 rows.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence - node3: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state, final full-cluster health\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b210a0092d984ad6\",\"cmd-ed636b206e06492f\",\"cmd-62a4ca9df8b848a3\",\"cmd-6e30c95397a54896\",\"cmd-6083fc1c389448c9\",\"cmd-c1ec9952b850486e\",\"cmd-d43e3a9a33a44017\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id=95e2f83d... with cluster_size=3/Synced/4 rows; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during reboot; post-reboot boot_id=5d228d3b... (changed); mariadb active again with cluster_size=3/Synced/4 rows; final cross-check from node1 confirms wsrep_incoming_addresses lists all three IPs and all 4 committed rows are intact cluster-wide.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Built a 3-member MariaDB Galera cluster (MariaDB 10.6.28 + galera-4) from scratch on node1/node2/node3 (RHEL7, no server packages pre-installed). Configured wsrep replication, opened firewalld Galera ports, bootstrapped the cluster, and loaded an application dataset (appdata.orders, 3 rows). Took the entire cluster down cleanly (node2, node3, then node1 last to guarantee safe_to_bootstrap), confirmed full outage, then restored it: bootstrapped node1 from its preserved grastate (seqno 9, safe_to_bootstrap:1) and rejoined node2/node3, recovering with all 4 committed rows (including a write made immediately before the outage) present and wsrep_cluster_size=3/Synced on every node. Then executed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured per-node boot_id + cluster/data health baselines, restarted node1, node2, and node3 one at a time via `sudo reboot` (never more than one down simultaneously), confirmed each node's boot_id changed, and verified each node auto-rejoined the cluster (size 3, Synced) with all 4 rows intact before moving to the next node.","actions_performed":["Diagnosed RHEL7 nodes had no MariaDB server, no repos configured, and a hung 'yum -q check' process holding the yum lock on each node","Killed the stuck yum lock-holder processes on node1/node2/node3","Added MariaDB 10.6 upstream repo and CentOS 7 vault base/updates/extras repos on all three nodes","Fixed corrupted rpmdb on node1 (rpm --rebuilddb) after the killed process left it inconsistent","Installed MariaDB-server, MariaDB-client, MariaDB-common, MariaDB-shared, galera on all three nodes","Opened firewalld ports 3306/4567(tcp+udp)/4568/4444 on all three nodes","Appended CLUSTER_HOSTS to /etc/hosts on all three nodes","Wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on each node with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3 and per-node wsrep_node_name/address","Bootstrapped Galera on node1 (galera_new_cluster) and started mariadb on node2/node3 to join via SST; confirmed wsrep_cluster_size=3, all Synced","Enabled mariadb.service on all three nodes for boot persistence","Created appdata.orders table and inserted 3 baseline rows plus 1 pre-maintenance-window row (4 total), confirmed replicated to all nodes","Performed a full ordered shutdown of the cluster (node2, node3, then node1 last) for the maintenance window; confirmed node1 grastate.dat had safe_to_bootstrap: 1 and all three nodes fully down (no mysqld processes)","Restored the cluster: galera_new_cluster on node1, then started mariadb on node2 and node3; verified wsrep_cluster_size=3/Synced and all 4 committed rows present on every node","Captured pre-restart boot_id and cluster/data health baseline on all three nodes","Restarted node1, node2, node3 sequentially via backgrounded 'sudo reboot', polling each until reachable again","Verified each node's boot_id changed after its restart and that each node auto-rejoined the Galera cluster (size 3, Synced) with all 4 rows intact before restarting the next node"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: 3-member Galera cluster running with application data before maintenance","command_ids":["cmd-4ff238ca27eb4dd7","cmd-0bafb7e9ae1642c6","cmd-8b2c407a8dda4543","cmd-594933ae1e6b4022","cmd-d2f9e48afeed4368","cmd-6cd049383f2647ec","cmd-d91e79300df74e93"],"summary":"All three nodes report wsrep_cluster_size=3 and Synced; appdata.orders table created on node1 with 3 rows replicated to node2/node3, then a 4th 'last-write-before-maintenance' row committed on node1 just before shutdown."},{"requirement":"Full cluster shutdown for the maintenance window","command_ids":["cmd-3b25417a893b41a8","cmd-b65b0cc7790349c5","cmd-2859abb1d8d046c9","cmd-fb64af3b5a4346a0","cmd-8ca142eecfae449b","cmd-e2da